The issue is caused by incorrect interpretation of the Pricing api. Proposing to clarify & refactor the api to avoid such situation in future:

We need:

# timestamps: driver arriving to client, driver starting driving with client , order finished - start.arrival_timestamp, start.departure_timestamp, final.arrival_timestamp
# start and end location - passing to tracking, used for fixed route checks - start.lat/lng, final.lat.lng
# approximate route taken - we use it to reestimate the route in case of gps issues - start + waypoints + final
# time spent at the stops - we charge paid wait rate based on the time - waypoints.departure_timestamp - waypoints.arrival_timestamp
# gps_lat/lng - we pass it to tracking call , needed for some fraud checks it seems
# to know if this is a multiple destinations ride - to disable fixed route - waypoints.length > 0

Proposed API:

{noformat}export interface Test {
    pickup: {
        lat: number;
        lng: number;
        gps_lat?: number;
        gps_lng?: number;
        arrival_timestamp: number;
        departure_timestamp: number;
    };
    extra_stops: Array<{
        lat: number;
        lng: number;
        arrival_timestamp: number;
        departure_timestamp: number;
    }>;
    dropoff?: {
        lat: number;
        lng: number;
        arrival_timestamp: number;
    };
};{noformat}

