h3. Mapping – Ride-hailing

+*1. Rider overcharges*+

Affected processes: 

* generic overcharge, all from [Rider Price Issues|https://support.taxify.eu/hc/en-us/sections/360004064619-Rider-Price-Issues] should be considered (there may be overlap with other types of automations)
* any case where the rider reports they have been overcharged
* rules are the same for all affected processes, so we could use the same content across all articles

Confluence info:

Automatically compensating Riders when they report they have been overcharged for a ride.

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
The compensation is in the form of a targeted campaign - 3 different “sizes” for each country. Possible campaigns are listed [here|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1XOtmMOfglBQBBisoDWSpKL86P5B9_GzD2AtWw5u2IAA/edit?usp=sharing].
{panel}

Conditions:

* Rider has not had the same compensation in last {{30 days}}
* Order states:
** {{finished}}
* Payment methods:
** {{inapp}}
** {{cash}}
* Order price review is not in progress
* Overcharge amount is less than S, M or L sized compensations
* Compensate if there wasn’t an overcharge (with a S promo)

+*2. Ride did not happen*+

Affected processes: 

* Ride did not happen
* important: info not to double refund

Confluence info:

* Automatically refunding a finished ride for which the Rider reported they were not in the car.

{panel:bgColor=#fffae6}
The refund is a “rider only” refund meaning that the rider gets their money back, but the driver balance is not hit.
{panel}

Conditions: 

Rider has not had any order refunds in last {{30 days}}

* Order states:
** {{finished}}
* Payment methods:
** {{inapp}}
* Order age < {{3 days}}
* Order value < {{20€}}

{quote}The refund button is still visible in old Admin, what happens if I refund the order again?{quote}

{panel:bgColor=#fffae6}
Please do not attempt to refund the order again. The Driver balance should only be hit if there are repeat reports against them.
{panel}

+*3. Cancellation fee*+

Affected processes: 

* Ride did not happen
* Cancellation fee overcharge

Confluence info:

Automatically refunding for a *cancelled* order where a cancellation fee was charged.

{panel:bgColor=#fffae6}
The refund is a “rider only” refund meaning that the rider gets their money back, but the driver balance is not hit.
{panel}

Conditions:

* Order states:
** {{client_cancelled}}
** {{cient_did_not_show}}
* Payment methods:
** {{inapp}}

{quote}The refund button is still visible in old Admin, what happens if I refund the order again?{quote}

{panel:bgColor=#fffae6}
Please do not attempt to refund the order again. The Driver balance should only be hit if there are repeat reports against them.
{panel}

