Hii, [~accountid:5b2bb5688ed0a74e47a94763]\!

_Driver Price Reviews_ does not seem to be assigned to me 🙈 Could you double-check, please? It seems to be published 14 days ago, would you like me to check that version?

Agree 100% with: 

{quote}_What seems to make sense is to possibly keep the stand-alone articles for_ [_🔒 Driver Unhappy with (Completed) Price Review_|https://support.taxify.eu/hc/en-us/articles/360013134459--Driver-Unhappy-with-Completed-Price-Review] _and_ [_🔒 Driver Is Checking Status of a Trip Payment or Price Review_|https://support.taxify.eu/hc/en-us/articles/360013134339--Driver-Is-Checking-Status-of-a-Trip-Payment-or-Price-Review] _but place both in the PR section._

Then, the information for Client did not pay/paid less either be put into the _Completing PR_ article (I think this is the best option) or they become a stand-alone article{quote}

I ended up writing rather long-ish feedback on the _Completing a Price Review_ article, please find it below (and if anything is unclear, do tag me\!). I’m sorry it’s so long haha, overall it’s good (and a clear improvement from what was), but we can make it even better ⭐ 

----

General observations:

* We do not put full stops at the end of bullet point sentences (even if it’s the last one from a list of bullet points), please delete those. The exception is if one bullet point has multiple sentences within itself.
* Inconsistent formatting – compare Fraud result and Status updates drop-downs. The first sentence either has to have a bullet point format or not. I’d lean towards not 🙂 It can look quite neat.
* Please replace all hyphens with en-dashes, as per the style guide

Detailed feedback:

*Step 1*

{quote}Check the _Price review reason_ and drivers comment supporting their reason{quote}

Apostrophe missing by the word “drivers”. Repetition of “reason”; can we rephrase? (i.e. their side of the story or something to this effect).

{quote}Check the _To driver_ rating and accompanying comment to understand the rider's experience{quote}

Maybe we could rephrase, to include the statement “rating left by rider”, just to be extra clear :)

{quote}Check the route map for assisting information.{quote}

Delete the word “assisting”, not needed.

In the drop-down *Route information*, there is an empty bullet point at the end.

{quote}Check that time gaps are appropriate{quote}

This is a bit unclear to me.

{quote}Check the _Calculation hint_ and estimated price - compare this to the amount the driver collected/is asking for{quote}

Why did you use the word “collected”? Maybe “earned” would be more fitting, or I am missing something haha

{quote}*Note*: If the information is not clear enough, call the driver to confirm trip details.{quote}

Here, I’d defo add – do not send an outgoing ticket.


Overall, Step 1 is missing a drop-down with a list of reasons for a price review – like automatic, driver requested etc, maybe we can add that too? I can see it is further down in the process, so actually, maybe we can restructure a bit – because this info can come in handy when checking the order first? I am not sure, honestly, I’ve never done a PR myself. Maybe we can get feedback from an agent who does them on a daily basis if you think that would help 🙂 

*Step 2*

{quote}Using the information collected from step 1, decide if the following is true:{quote}

Alright, but we do not have any instruction for “if the following is true, then…”, “if it’s false, then…”.

Word “Step” should be capitalised.

{quote}The price review is justified - if not, proceed to step *x* to finish the review{quote}

Missing the step number.

{quote}Select the _Send to order_ button - this will prefill the _Total driver price without toll roads and booking fees_ field.{quote}

Suggest rephrasing the word “prefill”, maybe “update” would suit better?

{quote}If the review needs further investigation or you are calling the user to confirm additional information, change this to _Not solved_{quote}

I feel like this is relevant in the note in step 1, maybe we can add it somewhere? :)

*Reason drop-down*, something is off with the formatting there (you have 3 empty bullet points at the end of the text). Could you edit it a bit so that there are not so many sub-paragraphs? The whole offline trip investigation could be a separate drop-down or even a stand-alone process (maybe we can incorporate it into _Driver Price Review Issues_ article).

{quote}This amount should already be populated from the route editor (see step 3){quote}

“Step” should be capitalised, and “populated” maybe a bit too difficult of a word here. “Updated”?

General question: is “Comment” field compulsory or not? We should indicate that.

{quote}*ABOUT PRICE TOO HIGH REVIEWS*{quote}

Not sure how I feel about all caps in a blockquote 😃 Maybe too much, it is pretty visible already.

