I would like to check with you a few things.

*1 Changing the order of ENUM value*

Changing ENUM can cause a lot of issues while the table is being altered. 

For example, in {{taxify_delivery_order}}.{{order}}

enum orders:

{noformat}`state` enum('waiting_acceptance','waiting_preparation','waiting_delivery','delivered','rejected' ,'failed') NOT NULL DEFAULT 'waiting_acceptance'{noformat}

Your request is add in enum in between existing enum

{noformat}req: `state` ENUM('waiting_acceptance','waiting_preparation','waiting_delivery',   <'ready_for_pickup','completed',>   'delivered','rejected' ,'failed') NOT NULL DEFAULT 'waiting_acceptance'{noformat}

This will make different internal value of enum and online schema change tool may refuse to alter at all.

Not to mention the entire data in the table will be re-written because of internal value changes.

I am asking you when adding enum value, add them sequentially like below

Example:

{noformat}`state` ENUM('waiting_acceptance','waiting_preparation','waiting_delivery','delivered','rejected' ,'failed','ready_for_pickup','completed') NOT NULL DEFAULT 'waiting_acceptance'{noformat}

It will avoid internal value changes, therefore tool does not need to re-write the data.

Please have a look again the following requested column:

{{taxify_delivery_order}}.{{order.state}}

{{taxify_delivery_order}}.{{order_state_log.to_state}}

{{taxify_delivery_order_africa}}.{{order.state}}

