Thank you for quick request review.{color:#333333} 
{color}
* {color:#333333}As part of the services, was there an obligation for them to provide a minimum amount of exposure to Bolt at a certain number of events or commitment to a certain number of people etc (ie any measurable performance requirement) that they are now failing to meet/in breach of?{color} 
{color:#333333} _No._{color}{color:#333333}
{color}
* {color:#333333}Is there the inclusion of a provision of force majeure?{color}

{color:#333333} _Yes, but a very general one:_{color}
 _{color:#333333} _6.3._{color} Force majeure circumstances - “force majeure”, the Parties understand and, for violations of the Agreement or its individual terms, caused by these circumstances, both Parties shall be liable in accordance with the provisions of the Civil Code of the Republic of Lithuania._
{color:#333333}{color}

{color:#333333} _The other which may be relevant, is:_{color}
 _2.1.1. The Parties clearly understand and hereby confirm that when the Arena is hosting events and the advertising of the certain event and / or advertising spaces in the Arena are organized by the promoters of a certain event,  *OR advertising in the Arena (* promotional campaigns or distribute promotional materials in the Arena), *due to the Arena's obligations to third parties, the specifics of the event, violations of legal acts  +or other circumstances+  are not possible to carry out,* during such events the relevant services in accordance with The Contract will not be provided to the Customer (Bolt) or the services already started  *will be suspended.*_{color:#333333}
{color}
* {color:#333333}When you suspended the agreement the first time, what did you discuss with them? Was this formalized in an amendment? Did they reduce the term of the agreement given or admit their failure to perform?{color}
{color:#333333}As far as I know (I've joined Bolt a bit later, in June), since Arena could not have any events, therefore, to provide advertising services anymore, it was clear for both sides that the suspension is the right thing to do in that situation. We did not pay for the services during quarantine months, they did not advertise us. So we had an amendment where the Parties agreed:{color}
 _1.1. Considering that due to the declared emergency situation in Lithuania and the quarantine introduced by the Government of the Republic of Lithuania, the activities of the Parties because of this regime are disrupted, the Parties agree to temporarily suspend the performance of the Agreement and the provision of the services referred in the Agreement._
 _1.2. The Parties confirm that the execution of the Agreement is suspended from 2020 March 16 to the end of the quarantine regime introduced by the Government or, before the abolition of the quarantine regime, if the prohibitions and restrictions on activities and events will be eliminated by the Government._  _The parties also have the right to enter into a written agreement_  _on the resumption of the provision of services in the event of an earlier decision to perform the Contract._
 _1.3. The agreement expires the day after the abolition of the quarantine regime is introduced by the government or, if the prohibition and restriction on the activities and events applicable to the Arena expire before the quarantine regime has been abolished,_


 _After the quarantine we've got into situation which was not written in the amendment – the quarantine had been cancelled but the restrictions on the event activities were still put on (at first, no events could happen inside, then inside events allowed but with a really limited audience, like 100-300 people when the capacity is 9000). So they wanted to start charging us for the services according to the amendment but we managed to postpone the continuing the services until there were no huge restrictions on the events, they agreed (this was a written request sent by email, they agreed)._{color:#333333} 
{color}
* {color:#333333}Is the only termination option a mutual agreement? Is there a clause stating for immediate termination in case of a breach? Any further wording to how the parties could separate? Are you under the impression they will be open to this without penalty to us?{color}
{color:#333333} _If the termination is before the expiration date with no breach, then yes, a mutual agreement is the option._{color}
{color:#333333} _In case of a breach, there is 4.4.:_{color}
 _4.4. If one of the Parties fails to fulfill its obligations under this Agreement or performs them improperly, the other Party shall submit in writing a claim for a breach. If the improperly performing Party does not start to properly perform obligations or does not correct violations within 5 (five) working days from the claim, the other Party shall have the right to terminate this Agreement by giving written notice to the breaching Party before 10 (ten) calendar days. Upon termination of the Agreement on the basis of this clause, the faulting Party, as soon as possible, but in any case no later than within 3 (three) calendar days upon receipt of the notification, shall pay the other Party a fine of EUR 250 (two hundred and fifty euros) and reimburse all other Direct losses incurred by a party, to the extent that they are not covered by the fine paid._{color:#333333}{color}{color:#333333}
{color}
* {color:#333333}Is there any clauses speaking to a right to reduce the services/fees or is it just a bulk service for the set fee?{color}
{color:#333333} _No, no clauses on reduction of services or fees. The price is also fixed for this bulk of service that we have and not detailed for each advertising line._{color}{color:#333333} 
{color}
* {color:#333333}How much money have we invested into this project? It seems to me that we have fulfilled in good faith all of our obligations under the agreement?{color}
{color:#333333} _It's 800 Eur / month + VAT and we're paying according to the schedule. So 2019 March (half) - 2020 March (half) plus September and October = (12 + 2 months ) * 800 eur = 11 200 Eur + VAT._{color}
