All, please note that just because a contract was not signed that it does not mean a contract was not created. Contracts don’t need to be written. Of course, we would rather have contracts that are written and signed as this ensures both parties have the same understanding of the exchange, but negotiations through email, phone calls, actions etc can all amount to the creation of a ‘contract’ between the parties. 

In order to understand better how to advise you here, please provide me with the following:

* A clear explanation of the services requested and the services actually received; 
* Any emails or written exchanges on the services;
* The draft agreement was not signed and the communication around it;
* Explanation of what the cost is that they are requesting now and what basis they are claiming (are they relying on the contract? Did the contract have some set term?) 

My impression is that because you did pay the invoices and service were provided at some point that there will be _some_ kind of contractual obligations. Now we just need to assess to what extent and whether they are binding.

